# Files that change how this project is reviewed, built, secured, or what its
# data must satisfy.
#
# Declared, not yet enforced. With one maintainer, the author of every pull request
# and the only code owner are the same person, and an author cannot approve their
# own pull request -- so requiring code-owner review would block all merges. It is
# switched on when outside contributions start.
#
# These matter more than most files because Copilot reads its review instructions
# from the pull request's own branch: editing them changes the review of that same
# pull request.

/.github/copilot-instructions.md    @tkakkie
/.github/instructions/              @tkakkie
/.github/workflows/                 @tkakkie
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @tkakkie
/AGENTS.md                          @tkakkie
/deny.toml                          @tkakkie
/migrations/                        @tkakkie
/docs/architecture/invariants.md    @tkakkie
/docs/security/                     @tkakkie
